sarah: Fixed and pushed. Replaced naive `await client.generate(...)` with this snippet: ```js
// simple retry with exponential backoff + Retry-After
async function safeGenerate(client, opts) {
  const maxAttempts = 4;
  for (let i = 0; i < maxAttempts; i++) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(opts);
    } catch (err) {
      const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
      if (retryAfter) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, retryAfter * 1000));
      } else if (i < maxAttempts - 1) {
        const backoff = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** i + Math.floor(Math.random() * 300), 8000);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
      } else {
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

ekaterina: Looks good. Add one line explaining why prefer trimming prefix vs dropping messages: "prefer selective prefix trimming (system + recent user messages kept) to preserve safety/context."

sarah: Added. The 3-bullet checklist now reads: "Cause: bursty traffic or long contexts; Immediate action: implement retry with Retry-After + trim oldest non-essential messages; Follow-up: add prompt set to evals to catch regressions."

